<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Detailed Probability Model for Random Sabotage</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a comprehensive mathematical analysis of the probability that a team of optimal cooperators will accidentally play enough defector-coded action cards to trigger mission sabotage. This analysis demonstrates that the game mechanics provide crucial plausible deniability for defectors through the inherent randomness of the discard mechanism.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Single Card Play Probability</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When a cooperator receives a hand containing defector-coded action cards, they must discard one card and draw two replacement cards. Given that 2 out of 5 action card types are defector-coded, the probability of being forced to play a defector-coded card after discarding is:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=P(\text{both draws are defector-coded})=\left(\frac{2}{5}\right)^{2}=0.16" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>both draws are defector-coded</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=P(\text{both draws are defector-coded})=\left(\frac{2}{5}\right)^{2}=0.16</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This represents the fundamental probability that drives accidental sabotage in our game.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Event-Level Analysis</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The initial hand composition determines the number of potential discards in an event. Each player begins with one card of each type plus one random card, yielding two possible scenarios:</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SSx2.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Scenario 1: One Defector-Coded Card (60% probability)</h4>

<div id="A1.SSx2.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx2.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When the random card is cooperator-coded, the hand contains exactly one defector-coded card available for discard. The probability distribution for playing <math id="A1.SSx2.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> defector-coded cards in this event is:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-p=0.84" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.84</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-p=0.84</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{1}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{1}(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p=0.16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p=0.16</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{1}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{1}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0\quad\text{for }k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0\quad\text{for }k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx2.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Scenario 2: Two Defector-Coded Cards (40% probability)</h4>

<div id="A1.SSx2.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx2.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When the random card is defector-coded, the hand contains two defector-coded cards available for discard. Using the binomial distribution for two independent discard opportunities:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.SSSx2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{2}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{2}(0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-p)^{2}=0.84^{2}=0.7056" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0.84</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7056</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-p)^{2}=0.84^{2}=0.7056</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{2}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{2}(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\binom{2}{1}p(1-p)=2\times 0.16\times 0.84=0.2688" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0.16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0.84</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2688</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\binom{2}{1}p(1-p)=2\times 0.16\times 0.84=0.2688</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{2}(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{2}(2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p^{2}=0.16^{2}=0.0256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0.16</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p^{2}=0.16^{2}=0.0256</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Aggregate Event Probability</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The overall probability distribution for a single event, accounting for both hand composition scenarios, is:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{event}}(k)=P(\text{Scenario 1})\cdot P_{1}(k)+P(\text{Scenario 2})\cdot P_{2}(k)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>event</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Scenario 1</mtext><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Scenario 2</mtext><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{event}}(k)=P(\text{Scenario 1})\cdot P_{1}(k)+P(\text{Scenario 2})\cdot P_{2}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting the values:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\text{event}}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>event</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\text{event}}(0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0.6\times 0.84+0.4\times 0.7056=0.7862" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0.84</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0.7056</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7862</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.6\times 0.84+0.4\times 0.7056=0.7862</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\text{event}}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>event</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\text{event}}(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0.6\times 0.16+0.4\times 0.2688=0.2035" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0.16</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0.2688</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2035</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.6\times 0.16+0.4\times 0.2688=0.2035</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\text{event}}(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>event</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\text{event}}(2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0.6\times 0+0.4\times 0.0256=0.0102" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0.0256</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0102</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.6\times 0+0.4\times 0.0256=0.0102</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Mission-Level Distribution</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A complete mission consists of 5 independent events. To find the probability distribution for the total number of defector-coded cards played across all events, we convolve the single-event distribution with itself five times.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SSx4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the number of defector-coded cards played in event <math id="A1.SSx4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. The total number for the mission is:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\sum_{i=1}^{5}X_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\sum_{i=1}^{5}X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Since events are independent and identically distributed, we can compute the probability mass function of <math id="A1.SSx4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> through repeated convolution:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{mission}}(k)=P(S=k)=((P_{\text{event}})^{5})(k)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mission</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>event</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{mission}}(k)=P(S=k)=((P_{\text{event}})^{5})(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A1.SSx4.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Convolution Calculation</h4>

<div id="A1.SSx4.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx4.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We perform the convolution iteratively. After two events:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P^{(2)}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P^{(2)}(0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P_{\text{event}}(0)^{2}=0.7862^{2}=0.6181" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>event</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0.7862</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6181</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P_{\text{event}}(0)^{2}=0.7862^{2}=0.6181</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P^{(2)}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P^{(2)}(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\cdot P_{\text{event}}(0)\cdot P_{\text{event}}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>event</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>event</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\cdot P_{\text{event}}(0)\cdot P_{\text{event}}(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\times 0.7862\times 0.2035=0.3199" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0.7862</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0.2035</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3199</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\times 0.7862\times 0.2035=0.3199</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P^{(2)}(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P^{(2)}(2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P_{\text{event}}(1)^{2}+2\cdot P_{\text{event}}(0)\cdot P_{\text{event}}(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>event</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>event</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>event</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P_{\text{event}}(1)^{2}+2\cdot P_{\text{event}}(0)\cdot P_{\text{event}}(2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0.0414+0.0160=0.0574" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.0414</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.0160</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0574</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.0414+0.0160=0.0574</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx4.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx4.SSSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Continuing this process through all five events yields the final mission-level distribution:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx4.SSSx1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\text{mission}}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mission</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\text{mission}}(0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=0.3005\quad(30.05\%)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3005</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>30.05</mn><mo>%</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.3005\quad(30.05\%)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\text{mission}}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mission</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\text{mission}}(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=0.3889\quad(38.89\%)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3889</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>38.89</mn><mo>%</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.3889\quad(38.89\%)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\text{mission}}(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mission</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\text{mission}}(2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=0.2209\quad(22.09\%)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2209</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>22.09</mn><mo>%</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.2209\quad(22.09\%)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\text{mission}}(k\geq 3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mission</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\text{mission}}(k\geq 3)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=0.0898\quad(8.98\%)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0898</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8.98</mn><mo>%</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.0898\quad(8.98\%)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Sabotage Threshold Analysis</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The sabotage condition requires at least <math id="A1.SSx5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3|D|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3|D|</annotation></semantics></math> defector-coded cards to be played, where <math id="A1.SSx5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D|</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of defectors. For a team of all cooperators attempting to avoid sabotage:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(\text{accidental sabotage})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>accidental sabotage</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(\text{accidental sabotage})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P(S\geq 3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P(S\geq 3)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=3}^{\infty}P_{\text{mission}}(k)=0.0898" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mission</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0898</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=3}^{\infty}P_{\text{mission}}(k)=0.0898</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This 8.98% probability represents a significant chance of accidental sabotage, providing essential cover for actual defectors.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Implications for Game Balance</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The nearly 9% probability of accidental sabotage serves several crucial game design purposes:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Plausible Deniability</span>: Defectors can claim bad luck when playing defector-coded cards, as cooperators face non-trivial odds of doing the same.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Strategic Depth</span>: Cooperators must balance between avoiding defector-coded cards and maintaining efficient play patterns that don’t reveal their role.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Accusation Uncertainty</span>: The substantial probability of accidental sabotage makes accusations based solely on card plays unreliable, encouraging deeper behavioral analysis.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This mathematical foundation ensures that the game maintains tension and uncertainty even with optimal play, preventing degenerate strategies where roles become immediately obvious from card selection patterns alone.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.T2" class="ltx_table ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:443.2pt;height:650.4pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><div class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="width:650.4pt;transform:translate(-103.6pt,-103.6pt) rotate(-90deg) ;"><figure>
